Time Complexity:
O(n)

Space Complexity:
O(n)

Approach:
1. Create a HashSet to store visited elements
2. Traverse the array
3. For each element, check if it already exists in the HashSet
4. If it exists, return true
5. Otherwise, add the element to the HashSet
6. Continue until all elements are processed
7. If no duplicate is found, return false


class Solution {
    public boolean containsDuplicate(int[] nums) {
        HashSet<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
        for(int ele:nums){
            if(set.contains(ele)) return true;
            set.add(ele);
        }
        return false;
    }
}
